  "factor_name": "Defensive Relative Strength with Breadth Gate",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "((R20_i - median_cross_section(R20))/sigma20_i) * breadth_gate * (1 if R60_i>0 else 0.55)",
    "description": "Cross-sectional 20-day relative strength normalized by each asset's 20-day realized volatility. Strength is amplified when fewer than half of assets have positive 20-day returns, damped in strongly broad rallies, and reduced for assets below their own 60-day trend. All inputs use completed observations only."
